{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778938581,"nonce":"6fF38BaJpoIFkG3K254+cMsvNUA=","message":"Initial design stance before implementation planning: I think this should be treated as the canonical Mandible work ledger, not merely as a faster cache in front of git-bug. Mandible should own structured issue/work/comment/relationship/event state in SQLite, with git-bug as an import/export adapter and compatibility surface. That keeps normal reads/writes, graph projection, issue details, comments, session links, auth-request resolution links, and live UI updates out of the git-bug lock path.\n\nThe graph consequence is important: issue mode should project from ledger issues and typed relationships, not from ad hoc git-bug labels/body parsing at render time. Auth requests can then be rendered as resolution/action evidence attached to issue nodes in issue mode, while remaining first-class nodes in auth/work modes. Sessions can similarly split into historical issue work records versus live agent actors. I will spec the ledger and graph integration together so the backend model does not force another graph refactor later.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}